 "summary": "No existing Mathlib or TauCeti declaration covers the extended-real logarithmic energy kernel, its truncations, the bounded-rectangle log integrability lemma, or the empirical pair-sum identity; the closest TauCeti API (`interactionEnergy`/`potentialEnergy` in OptimalTransport/Wasserstein) takes real-valued kernels and cannot express the infinite collision cost. The PR reuses existing TauCeti infrastructure (`lowerSemicontinuous_lintegral_probabilityMeasure`, `empiricalMeasureOfFintype_toMeasure`, `EReal.iSup_sub_coe`, `EReal.sub_coe_add_eq_add_sub`) rather than re-deriving it.",
